{
 "name": "mod-keys-layout",
 "about": "Issue #19: a key is rebound with one press (click the row, press the key, done; the next row at once) and keeps working by position on any keyboard layout. Keys are named as on a US keyboard, as the vanilla Controls window does: not localised, so the key at Q on AZERTY reads Q. Shim input sends the SDL key events another layout would (the key at Q typing 'a'). Happy paths: the AZERTY key at Q binds and reads Q at once, the drop key on it reads Q too; three rows rebound back to back; Shift+W binds W; F13 and Scroll Lock are named (ScrL short to fit); binding the default resets it; the Game keys group lists the game's binds (no weapon attack rows: mouse binds are the game's Options > Controls), rebinds Skill 1 (keyboard keys replaced, mouse 4 kept, saved to controls.cfg) and half of the move axis; search finds its rows. Error paths: a second press after the bind does nothing, Esc cancels a capture (mod and game key) and keeps the key, typing in the search binds nothing, a closed group hides its rows, no key is ever asked to be named. controls.cfg is GameLab's own and is put back after the run (writes_controls).",
 "fixture": "town-paladin",
 "mods": [
  "hwplib",
  "hwplib-luck",
  "hwplib-classui",
  "weaponswap",
  "droptrade"
 ],
 "shim_input": true,
 "writes_controls": true,
